From c91fec58004750e1030f39ef85a54181887f747c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meldra Engineering <eng@meldra.ai>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:33:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remediate SEC-2026-001/002, zero-copy execution path, audit
 logging, TOGAF documentation baseline

Security
- SEC-2026-001: agent DQE tools built QueryJob without tenant_id/role,
  bypassing namespace scoping and evaluating RBAC against a hardcoded role.
  Tenant and role now bound from request ContextVars (not LLM-visible tool
  arguments, so prompt injection cannot cross a tenant).
- SEC-2026-002: /v1/query/explain is a data-touching path and now carries
  tenant and role like its sibling endpoints.
- assert_tenant_scoped(): fail-closed guard on SQL and Python executors,
  enforced by default outside dev/test. Unscoped jobs always audited.
- AST regression test fails the build if any QueryJob omits tenant/role.

Performance
- PERF-2026-003: zero-copy Arrow path when RBAC is provably a no-op;
  rbac_is_noop() fails closed on policy-store error. Payload registered
  once (join alias is now a view, not a second copy). Column projection
  pushdown added.

Correctness
- expire_snapshots() committed nothing while reporting success; now commits
  and hard-blocks on meldra.retention.min_days.
- optimize_table() had no memory ceiling; now refuses above 5M rows.
- Docstring claimed unconditional predicate pushdown; corrected.

Observability
- observability/audit_log.py: JSON-lines, UTC ISO-8601, secret redaction,
  synchronous flush on deny/error, append-only.

Hygiene
- Deprecated datetime.utcnow() replaced across 7 modules.
- Removed junk files committed at repo root.

Docs: 16-document TOGAF-aligned baseline under docs/.

Verified: 16/16 new tests pass; existing suite unchanged vs baseline
(69F/13E, all psycopg2 environment failures), passing 46 -> 62.
